export const ESSAY_OVERRIDES: EssayOverrideMeta[] = [
  {"slug":"are-catholics-and-protestants-both-christians","title":"Are Catholics and Protestants Both Christians?","excerpt":"Catholics and Protestants confess the same creeds and divided in the sixteenth century over authority, justification, the sacraments, and Mary and the saints. Each side's teaching is given here in words its own teachers wrote, with what has changed since and what has not.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"babies-or-believers-why-christians-baptize-differently","title":"Babies or Believers? Why Christians Baptize Differently","excerpt":"Christians agree that Christ commanded baptism and disagree about whether the children of believers should receive it. The disagreement is eighteen centuries old, each side has real texts, and it was once settled by drowning people.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"can-a-christian-be-rich","title":"Can a Christian Be Rich?","excerpt":"Jesus said harder things about wealth than most churches repeat, the church has never agreed on how far those words reach, and both the prosperity preacher and his proudest critic have something to answer for.","updated":"2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"can-a-christian-lose-their-salvation","title":"Can a Christian Lose Their Salvation?","excerpt":"The New Testament promises that no one can snatch a believer from Christ's hand and warns believers not to fall away, often in the same chapter. The church has four ways of holding both, and one thing to say to the person who is afraid.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"can-a-nation-be-christian","title":"Can a Nation Be Christian?","excerpt":"The argument over whether America was founded as a Christian nation usually skips the question underneath it, which is what the Bible would mean by the phrase and whether any country has ever passed the test.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"can-i-trust-my-feelings-about-god","title":"Can I Trust My Feelings About God?","excerpt":"Feelings about God can be produced on demand, and some of the strongest have been mistaken. They are also part of what Scripture calls faith. Jeremiah 17:9, the Psalms and a treatise Jonathan Edwards published in 1746 each refuse both a faith that is only feeling and a faith that despises it.","updated":"2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"can-you-be-good-without-god","title":"Can You Be Good Without God?","excerpt":"Unbelievers can be good, and the harder question is what makes anything good at all.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"christianity-was-never-western","title":"Is Christianity a White Man's Religion?","excerpt":"The charge is stronger than its usual answer: the cross did reach most of the world on the same ships as the chains. But the faith was Asian and African before Europe had heard of it, and the people it was used against kept it and judged their masters by it.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"did-christianity-copy-pagan-myths","title":"Did Christianity Copy Pagan Myths?","excerpt":"The claim that the story of Jesus was copied from Horus, Mithras and other pagan gods is older than the internet, and it can be checked against the ancient sources it seldom cites.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"did-god-choose-me-or-did-i-choose-god","title":"Did God Choose Me, or Did I Choose God?","excerpt":"Christians have argued for sixteen centuries over whether God chooses who will be saved or people freely choose him, and the churches that disagree about it still confess the same gospel.","updated":"2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"did-god-choose-who-would-be-saved","title":"Did God Choose Who Would Be Saved?","excerpt":"Paul wrote that God has mercy on whom he wills and hardens whom he wills, and Paul wrote that God desires all people to be saved. Five Christian traditions have tried to keep both sentences, and each of them is left with a question it can't fully answer.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"did-god-command-genocide","title":"Did God Command Genocide?","excerpt":"The Old Testament does say that God ordered Israel to destroy the peoples of Canaan, and a Christian who wants to answer the charge has to begin by reading those chapters as they stand.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"did-jesus-really-rise-from-the-dead","title":"Did Jesus Really Rise from the Dead?","excerpt":"The strongest alternatives to the resurrection are theft, the wrong tomb, visions and legend, and most of them first appear in the New Testament itself. Each explains something. What history can do with them, and where it has to stop, is narrower than either side usually admits.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"did-the-resurrection-happen","title":"Did the Resurrection Actually Happen?","excerpt":"Christianity has staked everything on the claim that Jesus of Nazareth rose bodily from the dead, and the evidence for that claim can be weighed by anyone willing to read it carefully.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"divorce-remarriage-and-the-church","title":"Divorce, Remarriage and the Church","excerpt":"Jesus spoke about divorce more severely than most churches now do, the church has read him in three different ways for most of its history, and it has managed to fail both the marriages it should have guarded and the people it should have protected.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"do-i-have-to-go-to-church-to-be-a-christian","title":"Do I Have to Go to Church to Be a Christian?","excerpt":"People leave churches because they were hurt, because of hypocrisy and because they were bored, and those reasons are mostly true. No one is saved by attendance. The New Testament still has no picture of a Christian alone by choice, and it speaks differently to the wounded.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"do-the-gifts-of-the-spirit-still-happen","title":"Do the Gifts of the Spirit Still Happen?","excerpt":"Tongues, prophecy and healing divide churches that confess the same Holy Spirit. Paul wrote three chapters to a church that had every gift and was misusing them, and those chapters still question the loud church and the quiet one alike.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"does-god-have-a-plan-for-my-life","title":"Does God Have a Plan for My Life?","excerpt":"Jeremiah 29:11, Romans 8:28 and Proverbs 3:5-6 are read in their settings, where each says something harder than the greeting card. Scripture says plainly that God governs; whether he has a route for each life that must be found is argued among Christians, and no wrong turn puts a person outside his care.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"does-prayer-change-anything","title":"Does Prayer Change Anything?","excerpt":"Scripture commands asking, records that some things happened because people asked, and keeps the prayers that were refused, including one prayed in a garden by Jesus himself.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"does-science-disprove-god","title":"Does Science Disprove God?","excerpt":"The war between science and faith is a story told in the nineteenth century, and Galileo and Darwin both went differently than the story says. Science has made one kind of god unnecessary. Whether it can rule on the God of the creeds is a different question.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"doubt-after-church-abuse","title":"Doubt After Being Abused by a Church Leader","excerpt":"Abuse by a pastor or church leader often leaves a person doubting God himself, and the Bible has a great deal to say to that doubt.","updated":"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"excavation-not-demolition","title":"Deconstructing Your Faith: What to Tear Down and What to Keep","excerpt":"Much of what people tear down when they deconstruct was never the Christian faith, and the work is learning to tell the difference.","updated":"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-christianity-good-for-women","title":"Is Christianity Good for Women?","excerpt":"Christians have often been bad for women and have used the Bible to do it, Jesus was not, and the record of his church runs both ways for reasons the church has to tell on itself.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-depression-a-spiritual-failure","title":"Is Depression a Spiritual Failure?","excerpt":"Many believers in the dark have been told to pray more and trust more. Elijah, the psalmists, Job and Paul went to the bottom and were not told it was their fault, and Scripture treats a person as dust and breath together, so prayer and a doctor were never rivals.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-divorce-ever-right-and-may-a-divorced-person-remarry","title":"Is Divorce Ever Right, and May a Divorced Person Remarry?","excerpt":"Jesus and Paul speak about divorce in five passages, and Christians who honor every one of them give three different answers about when a marriage may end and whether another may follow. All three agree on what to say to a person who is in danger.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-gambling-a-sin","title":"Is Gambling a Sin?","excerpt":"Scripture never names gambling. It speaks of the lot, of the wish to be rich, of the household and the neighbor, and Christians who read it have reached two answers that have stood side by side for centuries. One question both must answer is who pays.","updated":"2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-hell-real-and-is-it-fair","title":"Is Hell Real, and Is It Fair?","excerpt":"The old objection to hell is that no short life could deserve an endless punishment. The church has given three answers to it, and Jesus said more about the fairness of judgment than either side of the argument tends to remember.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-hell-real-and-is-it-forever","title":"Is Hell Real, and Is It Forever?","excerpt":"The church has always confessed a final judgment, and it has never spoken with one voice about what hell is like or how long it lasts.","updated":"2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-it-wrong-to-love-your-country","title":"Is It Wrong to Love Your Country?","excerpt":"Scripture treats love of country as a real good, and the kind of love it honors grieves a country's sins and names them.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-jesus-the-only-way","title":"Is Jesus the Only Way?","excerpt":"The claim that Jesus is the only way to God has been called arrogant since the second century. Read where it was first spoken, it is narrower and stranger than the slogan, and every alternative to it also tells most of the world that it is wrong.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-money-the-root-of-all-evil","title":"Is Money the Root of All Evil?","excerpt":"The Bible never says that money is the root of all evil. It says something harder: that the love of it is a root of many evils, in the poor as well as the rich, and that the first people Paul had in mind were religious teachers.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-the-bible-reliable-enough-to-build-a-life-on","title":"Is the Bible Reliable Enough to Build a Life On?","excerpt":"The evidence can show that the Bible we have is very nearly the Bible that was written and that its writers stood near the events, and it cannot show that what they wrote is true, which is a different question and the harder one.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-the-church-responsible-for-antisemitism","title":"Is the Church Responsible for Antisemitism?","excerpt":"From a second-century sermon to a reformer's tract of 1543 to the German churches of the 1930s, Christians taught contempt for the people of Jesus. The New Testament they quoted says something else, and Paul had warned Gentile believers against exactly this.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"is-the-god-of-the-old-testament-the-god-of-jesus","title":"Is the God of the Old Testament the God of Jesus?","excerpt":"In the second century a Christian named Marcion decided the God of Israel could not be the Father of Jesus and cut the Old Testament out of his Bible. The church refused him and kept the harder book, with its flood, its wars and its mercy, and the question he asked has not gone away.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"should-christians-drink-alcohol","title":"Should Christians Drink Alcohol?","excerpt":"The Bible calls wine a gift, warns against it in some of its most vivid lines, and honors people who never touch it. Christians who abstain and Christians who drink in moderation each have Scripture and a long history, and Romans 14 gives both of them an order.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"should-christians-ever-go-to-war","title":"Should Christians Ever Go to War?","excerpt":"Jesus told his followers to love their enemies and put away the sword, his church has prayed over armies for sixteen hundred years, and Christians who take both facts seriously have come to two different answers and one shared shame.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"should-christians-keep-the-sabbath","title":"Should Christians Keep the Sabbath?","excerpt":"The fourth commandment is the longest of the ten and the one Christians agree on least. Some hold that the Sabbath continues on Sunday, some that Christ fulfilled it and the day is free, and some that the seventh day still binds. Each view is given in its own confession's words, with a word for the tired.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"should-christians-support-the-death-penalty","title":"Should Christians Support the Death Penalty?","excerpt":"Genesis 9:6 grounds the penalty for murder in the image of God, and the murderer bears that image too. The case for the state's sword and the case against it are both as old as the church, and each has a question it would rather not be asked.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"should-the-church-stay-out-of-politics","title":"Should the Church Stay Out of Politics?","excerpt":"The church has been told to stay out of politics since a royal priest said it to Amos. It has failed in two opposite ways, by lending the cross to rulers and by keeping silent while neighbors were wronged, and four Christian traditions still disagree about where it should stand.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"should-women-preach","title":"Should Women Preach?","excerpt":"Christians who hold the same Bible in the same esteem disagree about whether women may preach and pastor, and the texts, the history and the best case on each side all have to be heard.","updated":"2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"the-children-rome-threw-away","title":"What the First Christians Did About the Children Rome Threw Away","excerpt":"When leaving an unwanted newborn outside was an ordinary Roman family decision, the first Christians refused to do it, and the history of that refusal still bears on how the church treats unwanted children and their mothers.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"the-council-of-nicaea-what-was-decided-in-325","title":"What Was Decided at the Council of Nicaea?","excerpt":"In 325 the bishops at Nicaea decided that Jesus Christ is God in the same full sense as the Father, and most of the world's churches still confess what they wrote.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"the-early-church-under-rome","title":"When the Church Had Nothing to Lose","excerpt":"For almost three centuries the church lived under an empire that could kill it whenever it chose, and how it lived and grew there is history a post-Christian America needs to learn.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"the-historical-jesus","title":"Was Jesus Real? What Historians Actually Know","excerpt":"Nearly every historian of the ancient world, believer or not, agrees that Jesus of Nazareth lived and was crucified under Pontius Pilate, and the evidence says more about him than most people expect.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"the-persecution-we-invented","title":"Is the American Church Really Being Persecuted?","excerpt":"Most of what American Christians now call persecution is the loss of a privileged place in the culture, and the New Testament teaches a different way to bear that loss than the one we have learned.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"the-rise-of-the-nones","title":"Why Are People Leaving the Church?","excerpt":"Millions of Americans have left the church since the 1990s, and many of them simply drifted away from a faith the church had made too thin to hold them.","updated":"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"was-america-founded-as-a-christian-nation","title":"Was America Founded as a Christian Nation?","excerpt":"A deeply Protestant people built a national government that declined to call itself Christian, and some of the Christians who fought hardest to keep church and state apart were Baptists.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-a-christian-owes-the-city","title":"What Does It Mean to Seek the Welfare of the City?","excerpt":"Jeremiah's command to seek the welfare of Babylon tells Christians what they owe the places where they live, and the church has had to learn it again from Carthage to Birmingham.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-christian-nationalism-is-and-is-not","title":"What Christian Nationalism Is, and What It Is Not","excerpt":"Christian nationalism is a fusion of Christian faith and national belonging, and it is a different thing from the love of country that Scripture assumes.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-happens-to-people-who-never-hear-the-gospel","title":"What Happens to People Who Never Hear the Gospel?","excerpt":"Christians confess that no one is saved apart from Christ, and most people who ever lived never heard his name. Scripture says who the Judge is and where he sends his church, and it leaves a silence that neither comfort nor fear is allowed to fill.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-is-the-lords-supper","title":"What Is the Lord's Supper?","excerpt":"Christians agree that Jesus gave his church a meal of bread and wine and commanded it to be kept, and they have disagreed for five hundred years about what he meant by four words spoken over the bread.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-post-christian-means","title":"What \"Post-Christian\" Actually Means","excerpt":"What has ended in America is Christendom, the old arrangement in which the culture handed people the faith, and Jeremiah's letter to the exiles shows the church how to live after it.","updated":"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-render-unto-caesar-actually-means","title":"What Did Jesus Mean by \"Render Unto Caesar\"?","excerpt":"Jesus said \"Render to Caesar\" in the temple during the last week of his life, when men who wanted him dead asked him whether to pay a Roman tax.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-romans-13-says","title":"What Does Romans 13 Say About Obeying the Government?","excerpt":"Romans 13 tells Christians to be subject to whoever governs, and, read in its place in Paul's letter, it also tells them what government is for.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-the-church-got-wrong-about-race","title":"What the Church Got Wrong About Race, and What Scripture Said All Along","excerpt":"American pulpits defended slavery and then segregation with open Bibles, while Black Christians read the same book and heard the God of the Exodus. The texts had been plain the whole time.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"what-the-original-audience-heard","title":"What the First Readers of the Bible Actually Heard","excerpt":"Every book of the Bible was first written to particular people in a particular place, and reading it well begins with hearing what they heard.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"who-decided-what-books-are-in-the-bible","title":"Who Decided What Books Are in the Bible?","excerpt":"The New Testament was gathered over about three centuries as the churches read its books aloud in worship, and the letters and lists that show how it happened can still be read today.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-are-there-so-many-denominations","title":"Why Are There So Many Denominations?","excerpt":"Jesus prayed that his followers would be one so that the world would believe, and the history of why they are not includes pride, slavery, honest conviction and a prayer that is still unanswered.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-didnt-the-bible-ban-slavery","title":"Why Didn't the Bible Just Ban Slavery?","excerpt":"The Bible never bans slavery outright, and the American Christians who defended slavery explained away the texts in that same Bible that condemned what they were doing.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-does-god-allow-evil","title":"Why Does God Allow Evil?","excerpt":"The argument from evil is the strongest case against God. Its older form claimed a contradiction and has been answered. Its newer form has not been refuted, and the Bible meets it with a man who was never told why and with a cross.","updated":"2026-11-22T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-does-god-allow-suffering","title":"Why Does God Allow Suffering?","excerpt":"Suffering is the hardest objection to the Christian faith, and the Bible faces it more squarely than many of its defenders do.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-does-god-feel-far-away","title":"Why Does God Feel So Far Away?","excerpt":"Feeling that God is far away is one of the oldest experiences in the Bible and in the church, and it has more than one cause.","updated":"2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-does-god-let-children-suffer","title":"Why Does God Let Children Suffer?","excerpt":"The suffering of children is the hardest form of the hardest question, and the Bible gives it lament, a cross and a promise where we wanted an explanation.","updated":"2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-jesus-wont-fit-in-either-party","title":"Why Jesus Won't Fit in Either Party","excerpt":"Both the right and the left have tried to make Jesus a member, and the long history of that temptation shows why he can't be handed to either one.","updated":"2026-11-20T00:00:00.000Z"},
  {"slug":"why-trust-the-bible","title":"Can You Trust the Bible?","excerpt":"The evidence for how the Bible was copied, collected and written is stronger than the rumors about it, and the question of trusting it finally comes to rest on Jesus.","updated":"2026-11-17T00:00:00.000Z"},
];
